  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nDue to the cold temperatures this morning, the growing season\nhas ended for most of northwestern PA and areas along the \nridge-line. Tonight, most of the area has a chance for frost\nwith some localized areas of freezing temperatures. A Frost\nAdvisory was issued for all areas still in the growing season\n(eastern Ohio, most of northern WV, and southwestern PA). Due \nto these colder overnight temperatures, there is another chance \nfor river valley fog to develop tomorrow morning.\n\nModel ensembles continue to indicate a stationary closed low \noff the Mid Atlantic/Carolina coast region through most of the \nweek along with a trough across the western CONUS. In between \nthese two systems, a ridge is forecast to persist across the \ncentral CONUS to the Upper Ohio Valley region during that time. This\nshould maintain dry weather across the area, with near \nseasonable high temperatures and slightly below average low\ntemperatures. \n\nA weak trough is progged to cross the area on the NE periphery \nof the ridge on Thursday. With surface high pressure in place, \nonly a slight decrease in temperature is expected by late week \nwith the lower 500mb heights.",
